<title>NETHERLANDS: DUTCH SHELL RAISES DIESEL PRICES.</title>
<headline>DUTCH SHELL RAISES DIESEL PRICES.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal Dutch/Shell unit Shell Nederland BV said on Friday it will raise its retail prices for diesel in the Netherlands by 1.0 cents per litre with effect from November, 18.</p>
<p>The move reflects changes in international product prices and the value of the dollar against the guilder, the company said.</p>
<p>From Monday the price diesel at Shell's self-service stations rises to 1.492 guilders per litre.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
